SKIP – The class `ObservableTimer` primarily delegates to a `Scheduler` to schedule a delayed emission. Its behavior depends on asynchronous timing and external thread‑pool resources, making it unsuitable for a deterministic JMH micro‑benchmark. Benchmarking such code would require controlling the scheduler (e.g., using a trampoline or immediate scheduler) and would not reflect the real‑world latency of the timer, so a JMH test would add little value.